pfSense GUI management plugin for Zapret2 DPI bypass.

Zapret2 (nfqws/tpws) is an open-source tool for circumventing deep packet
inspection (DPI) used by some ISPs to block or throttle specific services
such as YouTube, Discord, and Rutracker.

This package provides:
  - GUI page under Services → Zapret2
  - Profile-based configuration (safe / default / aggressive / custom)
  - Interface selection (LAN and OPT interfaces)
  - Per-target bypass control (YouTube, Discord, Rutracker, custom domains)
  - Service management (start / stop / restart / health check)
  - Status block with process info and recent log entries

NOTE: This is an MVP/experimental release.
The zapret2 backend (nfqws/tpws binaries) must be installed separately.
See INSTALL.md in the package repository.

WWW: https://github.com/your-org/pfSense-pkg-zapret2
